<!doctype html>
{% comment %}
  ============================================================================
  layout/suf.liquid — the layout for rebuilt pages.
  ============================================================================

  Selected per template, not globally. A JSON template opts in with a top-level
  key; a Liquid template with a tag:

      { "layout": "suf", "sections": { ... } }        <- JSON
      {% layout 'suf' %}                              <- Liquid

  templates/password.json already uses the JSON form for layout/password.liquid,
  which is the proof this works on a Vintage theme.

  WHAT THIS LAYOUT LOADS, AND WHY
  -------------------------------
  Net-new:  suf.css, suf.js.
  Legacy:   jQuery, dt-framework.css, dt-custom.css, dT_main.js, dT_main_app.js
            — and only because sections/suf-header.liquid still needs them.
            Each is fenced below and annotated.

  NOT loaded, deliberately: dt-plugins.js (Swiper), dt-theme.js, handlebars,
  select2 and its stylesheet, ajax-cart, lazysizes, swiper-bundle.min.css.
  That is roughly 470 KB that theme.liquid loads and this layout does not.

  Consequences, all intended:

  * NO CART DRAWER. The header cart icon falls back to its own href and goes to
    the cart page. New pages link straight to checkout, so the drawer is not
    wanted. The mobile NAV drawer still works, because its code is inline in
    the header section rather than in any file dropped above.
  * NO LAZYSIZES. Use native loading="lazy", not class="lazyload".
  * NO COOKIE BANNER yet. See docs/migration.md — resolve before any suf page
    is assigned to a live page handle.
  * Legacy sections other than the forked header render only as well as
    dt-framework.css happens to style them. Prefer suf-* sections here.

  The legacy block below is temporary and shrinks as sections/suf-header.liquid
  is reduced. Do not add to it — port the section instead. The reduction
  checklist is in docs/migration.md.
{% endcomment %}
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="{{ settings.primary_color }}">

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://cdn.shopify.com" crossorigin>

    {%- if canonical_url != blank -%}
      <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
      <link rel="shortcut icon" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32 }}" type="image/png">
    {%- endif -%}

    {% render 'SEO-tags' %}
    {% render 'social-meta-tags' %}

    {% comment %}
      Both weights are used above the fold -- 400 for body, 700 for headings and
      the header nav -- so both are preloaded. 27 KB for the pair.
    {% endcomment %}
    {{ 'hanken-grotesk-400.woff2' | asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'font', type: 'font/woff2', crossorigin: 'anonymous' }}
    {{ 'hanken-grotesk-700.woff2' | asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'font', type: 'font/woff2', crossorigin: 'anonymous' }}

    {% comment %}
      ---- LEGACY, FOR THE HEADER ONLY. See the note at the top of this file.
      Both stylesheets are Liquid-templated CSS rendered against merchant
      settings, so neither can be compiled into suf.css. They come off the
      moment the forked header stops depending on them.
    {% endcomment %}
    {{ 'dt-framework.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {{ 'dt-custom.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {% comment %} ---- end legacy CSS {% endcomment %}

    {% comment %} Loaded last so it wins the cascade against dt-framework. {% endcomment %}
    {{ 'suf.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

    {% comment %}
      Theme-editor values -> custom properties, after suf.css so they override
      the fallbacks compiled into it. Two separate sets on purpose: the brand
      palette for new components, and the inherited palette the forked header
      still needs. See each snippet for why they cannot be one.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% render 'suf-tokens' %}
    {% render 'suf-legacy-tokens' %}

    {% comment %}
      Hanken Grotesk is applied on this layout only. theme.liquid stays on Arial
      until the legacy templates have been reviewed -- see docs/migration.md.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% render 'suf-fonts', apply: true, family: "'Hanken Grotesk', Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" %}

    {% comment %}
      ---- LEGACY, FOR THE HEADER ONLY.
      jQuery is render-blocking on purpose: the header section contains an
      inline <script> that runs during parse and would throw without it. That
      inline script is plain jQuery — no plugins, no ajax, no animation — so it
      is portable to roughly 70 lines of vanilla. Doing that alone will NOT
      remove jQuery, because dT_main.js and dT_main_app.js are jQuery too.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% # theme-check-disable ParserBlockingScript %}
    <script src="{{ 'jquery-3.5.1.min.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
    {% # theme-check-enable ParserBlockingScript %}

    {% comment %}
      dT_main_app.js reads exactly these three strings, and nothing else, from
      the global that theme.liquid calls DT_THEME. Reproduced here rather than
      shared so this layout has no dependency on theme.liquid.
    {% endcomment %}
    <script>
      var DT_THEME = {
        strings: {
          viewMyWishList: "View my wishlist",
          minCompareProduct: {{ 'products.product.minCompareProduct' | t | json }},
          minCompareProductNav: {{ 'products.product.minCompareProductNav' | t | json }}
        },
        moneyFormat: {{ shop.money_format | json }}
      };
    </script>
    {% comment %} ---- end legacy head JS {% endcomment %}

    {% comment %}
      Required. Shopify injects analytics, app embeds and the theme editor
      bridge here. Removing it breaks the editor and app blocks.
    {% endcomment %}
    {{ content_for_header }}
  </head>

  <body class="suf-body template-{{ template | replace: '.', ' ' | truncatewords: 1, '' | handle }}">
    <a class="suf-skip-link" href="#suf-main">Skip to content</a>

    {% comment %}
      ---- LEGACY SCAFFOLDING, FOR THE HEADER ONLY.
      The header's inline JS targets these two elements by class and fills the
      first one with the mobile menu. They are empty markup, not behaviour, but
      the mobile nav does not open without them.
    {% endcomment %}
    <div class="mobile-menu" data-menu="dt-main-menu" id="dt-main-menu-panel"></div>
    <div class="mobile-menu-overlay"></div>

    {% section 'suf-header' %}
    {% comment %} ---- end legacy scaffolding {% endcomment %}

    <main id="suf-main" class="suf-main">
      {{ content_for_layout }}
    </main>

    {% section 'suf-footer' %}

    {% comment %}
      ---- LEGACY, FOR THE HEADER ONLY.
      The sticky predictive search. Between them these two cover all five of
      the search bar's DOM identifiers; dT_search.js and dT_SearchNew.js were
      the superseded implementations and are already deleted. Shopify's native
      /search/suggest.json makes replacing these a small fetch module rather
      than a 148 KB port — that is the step that finally drops jQuery.
    {% endcomment %}
    <script src="{{ 'dT_main.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
    <script src="{{ 'dT_main_app.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
    {% comment %} ---- end legacy body JS {% endcomment %}

    {% comment %} Net-new SUF scripts. Native ES module; type=module implies defer. {% endcomment %}
    <script src="{{ 'suf.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>
  </body>
</html>
